  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Programme Cooperation Agreement 2022-2025 CI and CLT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support toUNESCO&apos;s Medium Term Strategy in the specific areas of culture, communication and information. UNESCO&apos;s program for the period 2022-2025 has a general focus on Africa, and the funds this agreement contribuites to are targeting ODA-eligable countries. Gender equality is a global priority. The impact of the climate emergency on culture will also be addressed and the role of culture in climate change mitigation and adaptation will be strengthened.

Strategic Objective 3: Build inclusive, just and peaceful societies by promoting freedom of expression, cultural diversity, education for global citizenship, and protecting the heritage. 

Culture Sector (Major Programme IV) 
Outcome 5: Enhance the protection and promotion of the diversity of heritage and cultural expressions.

Communication and information (Major Programme V) 
Outcome 6: Promote freedom of expression and the right to information
Outcome 8: Foster knowledge sharing and skills development in the digital age
Outcome 9: Develop ethical standars, norms and frameworks for action to meet the challenges of innovative technologies and digital transformation</narrative>
  </description>
